{{also|Tribute|tributé}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|tréyes}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*-tós}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tribut}}, from {{der|en|fro|tribut}}, from {{der|en|la|tributum|t=tribute|lit=a thing contributed or paid}}, neuter of {{m|la|tributus}}, past participle of {{m|la|tribuō|t=to assign, allot}}, usually derived from {{m|la|tribus||tribe}}. See {{m|en|tribe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɹɪbjuːt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tribute.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[acknowledgment]] of [[gratitude]], [[respect]] or [[admiration]]; an [[accompanying]] [[gift]].
#: {{ux|en|Please accept this as a '''tribute''' of our thanks.}}
#* {{RQ:Gray Elegy|passage=the passing '''tribute''' of a sigh}}
## An [[homage]] made in a [[body of work]] to another work or [[creator]].
##: {{ux|en|Did you catch the ''Up in Smoke'' '''tribute''' in that episode of ''{{w|That '70s Show}}''?}}
# A [[payment]] made by one [[nation]] to another in [[submission]].
#: {{ux|en|The Ancient Romans made their conquered countries pay '''tribute'''.}}
# [[extortion|Extortion]]; [[protection]] [[money]].
# A payment made by a [[feudal]] [[vassal]] to his [[lord]].
# {{lb|en|mining}} A certain proportion of the mined [[ore]], or of its [[value]], given to the [[miner]] as [[payment]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1778|author=w:William Pryce|title=Mineralogia Cornubiensis: A Treatise on Minerals, Mines, and Mining{{...}}
|passage=The setting of a Copper Mine upon '''tribute''' , has this difference : the Tributor is at the sole expence of digging , raising , and dressing , all the Ore that can be made merchantable}}
#* '''1852-1866''', {{w|Charles Tomlinson (scientist)|Charles Tomlinson}}, ''Cyclopaedia of Useful Arts and Manufactures''
#*: Tut-work is also employed upon the lode itself, though from the advantages generally considered to arise from the '''tribute''' system{{...}}

====Usage notes====
* Often used in the construction ''pay tribute to''.

